        <briefdescription>
<para>Constructs the function object from a callable and the arguments. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Copies (or moves) the callable and the arguments into the object.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>C</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the callable, as passed. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>A</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The types of the arguments, as passed.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Constraints</title><para>At least one argument, so that the copy and move constructors are used for copies (there is always at least one stored argument, and the member initialisation requires one argument for each of them). The constraint does not refer to <computeroutput>Args_T</computeroutput>, since clang 17 and 18 crash on the out-of-line definition of a constraint that refers to the pack of the enclosing class.</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>callable</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The callable object. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>arguments</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The arguments passed to the callable after the leading reference.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The callable and the arguments are forwarded to the constructors of the members, which store decayed copies. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
