<simplesect kind="par"><title>Returns</title><para>Nothing.</para>
</simplesect>
A function, a function pointer, or a function object is called directly, not through <computeroutput>std::invoke()</computeroutput>, which, without optimisations, adds three frames to the call chain; a pointer to a member, which only <computeroutput>std::invoke()</computeroutput> can call, is still passed to it. </para>
