    <briefdescription>
<para>Function object that holds a callable and the additional arguments it is invoked with. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Returned by <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a6abb44ef8226b1f80aad8010b5ef1a5c" kindref="member">bind_callable()</ref></computeroutput> when there are additional arguments. When invoked with a <computeroutput>Self_T&amp;</computeroutput> reference, it invokes the stored callable with that reference, followed by the stored arguments, as non-<computeroutput>const</computeroutput> lvalues.</para>
<para>It replaces a lambda, since the function call operator of a lambda cannot be marked as always inlined in a way accepted by all the supported compilers; without optimisations, a separate frame for it would make the call chain of each nested test case longer.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Self_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type referred to by the first parameter of the callable (<computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1test__case" kindref="compound">test_case</ref></computeroutput> or <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1suite" kindref="compound">suite</ref></computeroutput>). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Callable_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the stored callable (decayed). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Args_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The types of the stored arguments (decayed). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
